---
/**
 * Privacy Policy. Draft. Needs a human read before launch.
 *
 * Written against what the site actually does, which is very little: one
 * contact form, no analytics, no cookies, no embeds. If any of that changes,
 * this page has to change with it in the same commit.
 */
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { business } from "../config/business";

const { form, email } = business.processors;
---

<Legal
  title={`Privacy policy: ${business.name}`}
  description="What our contact form collects, where it goes, how long we keep it, and how to have it deleted. We run no analytics and set no cookies."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  standfirst="This page says exactly what we collect and what we do with it. It is short because we collect very little."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    We collect what you type into the contact form. It is emailed to the three
    of us so we can reply. We do not sell it, we do not add you to a mailing
    list, and we do not track you while you read this site.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>The contact form asks for four things:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, so we know who we are replying to.</li>
    <li>Your email address, so we can reply at all.</li>
    <li>Your business name, so we can look you up before we call.</li>
    <li>
      What you need, so the person who answers is the one who does that kind of
      work.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A phone number is optional. Leave it blank and the form still works. We
    only use it if you tell us you would rather be called than emailed.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is one more field in the form that you never see. It is a hidden box
    called a honeypot. It stays empty when a person fills the form in, and
    automated spam tends to fill it, which is how we throw spam away. It
    collects nothing about you.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      No analytics. There is no Google Analytics, no Plausible, no Meta pixel
      and no session recording on this site. We do not know how many people
      read this page.
    </li>
    <li>
      No cookies. This site sets none. See the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>
      for the detail.
    </li>
    <li>
      No hidden capture of your IP address, the page you came from, or the
      browser you are using.
    </li>
    <li>
      No embedded third party content. No web fonts loaded from Google, no
      YouTube player, no map iframe, no chat widget. The font on this page is
      served from this website.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We run ads for clients. We have deliberately not put an advertising pixel
    on our own site.
  </p>

  <h2>Where your message goes</h2>
  <p>
    Two companies handle your message on the way to us, and only those two.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>{form.name}</strong> {form.role}. When you press send, the form
      posts straight to them and they forward it to our inbox. They keep a copy
      of submissions on their own systems. Their privacy policy is at
      <a href={form.privacyUrl} rel="noopener">{form.privacyUrl}</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{email.name}</strong> {email.role}. Your message sits in our
      mailbox the same way any email would. Their privacy policy is at
      <a href={email.privacyUrl} rel="noopener">{email.privacyUrl}</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nobody else sees it. We do not pass enquiries to other agencies, and we do
    not have an affiliate arrangement with anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    If you become a client, we keep your details for as long as we are working
    together and for two years afterwards, because that is roughly how long a
    question about old work takes to arrive.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you do not become a client, we delete the enquiry within twelve months.
  </p>

  <h2>Having your details deleted</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and ask. You
    do not need to give a reason and you do not need to use any particular
    wording. We will delete what we hold, tell you we have done it, and ask
    {form.name} to remove their copy too.
  </p>
  <p>
    Under the Texas Data Privacy and Security Act you can also ask us what we
    hold about you, ask us to correct it, and ask for a copy of it. Same
    address, same answer time, which is two business days for the reply and up
    to forty five days to finish the job.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site sells services to businesses. It is not aimed at children and we
    do not knowingly collect anything from anyone under thirteen.
  </p>

  <h2>If this page changes</h2>
  <p>
    The date at the top changes with it. If we ever add analytics or anything
    that sets a cookie, we will say so here before we turn it on, and the
    cookie policy will stop saying that we set none.
  </p>
</Legal>
